  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid in Response to the Cyclone in Myanmar and Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 14 May 2023, Cyclone Mocha made landfall near the Bangladesh-Myanmar border. While Cox&#x2019;s Bazar was largely spared the full force of the cyclone, intense and heavy wind and rainfall destroyed and damaged shelters, water points, latrines, culverts, bridges and other key community infrastructure in the Rohingya refugee camps, including those under the International Organization for Migration (IOM)&#x2019;s Area of Responsibility. The Government of Bangladesh declared a &#x201c;Danger Signal 10&#x201d; in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar and neighboring coastal districts. Three flags &#x2013; the highest warning signal &#x2013; were hoisted in the camps of Cox&#x2019;s Bazar and neighboring areas.IOM conducted preparedness work on a &#x2018;no regret&#x2019; basis prior to landfall in coordination with authorities, humanitarian agencies and Rohingya community volunteers, and continues to respond to the needs on the ground. As such, under this project, IOM is providing lifesaving water, sanitation and health (WASH) services for Rohingya refugees and vulnerable members of the host community in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar district who were affected by Cyclone Mocha.</narrative>
  </description>
